"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[3995],{10544:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"init","desc":"Bootstrap hook. Adopts every existing `Vehicle`-tagged model and subscribes to\\nlater additions.\\n\\nNo-ops entirely when the `Vehicle` feature flag is off.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":215,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"start","desc":"Bootstrap hook. Subscribes to `VEHICLE_START_CONTROL`, the action the server\\ndispatches when this player takes or leaves the driver\'s seat. Taking control\\nhides the enter prompt and starts the physics loop; releasing it does the\\nreverse.\\n\\nNo-ops entirely when the `Vehicle` feature flag is off.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":240,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"setupCar","desc":"Adopts `car` as the vehicle this client controls: resolves every instance the\\nphysics loop needs, measures the steering geometry, resets all motion state,\\nand wires the lifetime listeners.\\n\\nExpects a specific model layout \u2014 `DriverSeat`, `Chasis/Platform/Engine`, the\\nfour `Cylindrical*` wheel motors on the engine, `SpringAttachmentF*` on the\\nplatform, and a `Flight` folder holding the submarine constraints. Every\\nlookup is a `WaitForChild`, so a model missing any of these **hangs here\\nrather than erroring**.\\n\\nSteering geometry is derived from the live attachment positions rather than\\nhard-coded: track width from the two front spring attachments, wheelbase from\\nfront-left to rear-left. Both use `Magnitude`, so they hold regardless of how\\nthe model is oriented when this runs.\\n\\nThe car is un-anchored at the end \u2014 models are spawned anchored so they cannot\\ndrift before their constraints are configured.\\n\\nThe initial state is chosen from the character\'s `Swimming` attribute, and a\\nlistener keeps it in sync afterwards. Transitions *out* of water deliberately\\nwait 0.4s (guarded by `switchingState`) so the vehicle does not snap back to\\ndriving mode while it is still breaching the surface.\\n\\n**Yields** on the `WaitForChild` calls.","params":[{"name":"car","desc":"The vehicle model to adopt","lua_type":"Model"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":292,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"setState","desc":"Switches the vehicle between `driving` and `submarine`. No-ops if already in\\nthat state.\\n\\nThe two modes are mutually exclusive by construction: the four flight\\nconstraints are enabled only for `submarine`, and wheel `MotorMaxTorque` is\\nset to the full torque for `driving` and to **zero** otherwise. Zeroing torque\\nrather than disabling the constraints leaves the wheels free-spinning, which\\nis what lets a submarine coast rather than dragging its brakes.\\n\\nBefore switching, the target orientation is seeded from the vehicle\'s current\\nworld orientation so a submarine does not snap to an arbitrary heading the\\ninstant it enters the water.","params":[{"name":"state","desc":"`\\"driving\\"` or `\\"submarine\\"`","lua_type":"VehicleTypes.CarState"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":454,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"updateSubPhysics","desc":"Recomputes the submarine rig from the vehicle\'s current mass.\\n\\n`subForce` is exactly `mass * gravity` \u2014 the force the anti-gravity\\n`VectorForce` must apply to hold the vehicle neutrally buoyant, so vertical\\ncontrol becomes a signed offset around zero rather than a fight against\\ngravity. The station-keeping `AlignPosition` gets a quarter of that, deliberately\\nweak so it holds position without fighting the movement force.\\n\\nWhile in submarine mode it also re-anchors the hold position to where the\\nvehicle actually is, so the rig never tries to drag it back to a stale point.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":529,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"updateTorque","desc":"Recomputes wheel torque from the vehicle\'s mass and applies it to the seat and\\nall four motors. Re-runs whenever the platform\'s `AssemblyMass` changes \u2014 that\\nis, whenever a passenger boards or leaves \u2014 so a loaded vehicle does not\\nbecome sluggish.\\n\\nTorque is `MAX_SPEED * mass * 1.3`: sizing torque against mass keeps\\nacceleration roughly constant regardless of load, and the 1.3 is headroom for\\nslopes. Each occupant additionally adds a flat 100 to the mass estimate,\\nbecause character assemblies are not part of the vehicle\'s `AssemblyMass`.\\n\\nAlways calls [VehicleController.updateSubPhysics] first \u2014 which is also what\\nre-reads the true assembly mass \u2014 then returns early unless the state is\\n`driving`, since torque means nothing in submarine mode.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":569,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"startControl","desc":"Takes control of the vehicle: binds the physics loop to Heartbeat, refreshes\\ntorque, raises `ClientState.inVehicle`, reconfigures the camera for driving\\n(classic mode, wide zoom range, subject back on the humanoid) and plays the\\nseatbelt SFX.\\n\\nIt also binds a sink action over the gameplay inputs that would otherwise fire\\nwhile driving \u2014 left click, `E`, `R`, `G` and the equivalent gamepad buttons.\\nRight mouse button is deliberately **not** sunk, because that is camera orbit.\\n\\nCalled from the `VEHICLE_START_CONTROL` subscription, not directly.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":632,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"stopControl","desc":"Releases control: zeroes every throttle and steering input, holds all four\\nwheels at zero angular velocity with full torque (so the vehicle brakes and\\nstays put rather than rolling away driverless), clears\\n`ClientState.inVehicle`, and unbinds the input sink.\\n\\nFinally it reports the distance travelled to the server via\\n`VEHICLE_LOG_DISTANCE` and resets the counter \u2014 dismounting is the only time\\nthe odometer is flushed, so a client that never dismounts never banks the\\nstat.\\n\\nCalled both from the `VEHICLE_START_CONTROL` subscription and from the car\'s\\n`Destroying` handler.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":696,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"updateCar","desc":"One frame of car physics. Called by [VehicleController.update] while the state\\nis `driving`.\\n\\n**Steering.** The seat\'s `SteerFloat` is scaled to `MAX_STEER_ANGLE` and\\napproached exponentially rather than snapped. The approach rate itself scales\\nwith speed (8 at idle up to 38 at full throttle), so parking manoeuvres feel\\nweighty while highway corrections feel sharp. Both front spring attachments\\nare then oriented to the resulting angle \u2014 this is the Ackermann knuckle\\nrotation; the wheels themselves are driven separately below.\\n\\n**Throttle.** `ThrottleFloat` is approached at `THROTTLE_ACCELERATION` and\\nclamped to \xb11, then multiplied by `MAX_SPEED` and the car\'s `SpeedMultiplier`\\nattribute (set by the server from the vehicle\'s upgrades). Below 10% input the\\nthrottle bleeds toward zero, which is the engine-braking feel \u2014 releasing the\\nkey coasts to a stop instead of freewheeling.\\n\\n**Differential.** Rather than computing true Ackermann per-wheel speeds, the\\ninner wheels are simply slowed proportionally to steering lock (up to 60% at\\nfull lock). The resulting speed difference across the axle produces a yaw\\nmoment that helps the car rotate, which is cheaper and more forgiving than\\ngeometric Ackermann on Roblox\'s constraint solver. Right-side wheels take the\\nnegated speed because they face the opposite way.\\n\\n**Odometer.** Per-frame displacement is accumulated, ignoring sub-0.1-stud\\ndeltas so physics jitter on a parked car does not inflate the total.","params":[{"name":"deltaTime","desc":"Frame delta from Heartbeat","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":781,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"updateSubmarine","desc":"One frame of submarine physics. Called by [VehicleController.update] while the\\nstate is `submarine`.\\n\\nUnderwater the camera *is* the control surface. Steering input yaws the camera\\n(lerped, not snapped), the vehicle\'s `AlignOrientation` then chases the\\ncamera\'s heading, and the camera\'s **pitch** \u2014 offset by\\n`THROTTLE_VERTICAL_DEGREE_OFFSET` and normalized against\\n`THROTTLE_MAX_VERTICAL_DEGREE` \u2014 becomes the dive/climb command. Looking down\\nwhile accelerating dives; looking up climbs. Vertical speed is scaled by\\nthrottle magnitude, so pointing the camera down while stationary does nothing.\\n\\nThrottle and steering both ease toward their goals and bleed back to zero\\nbelow 10% input, the same engine-braking feel as the car. All submarine speeds\\nare additionally scaled by `SUBMARINE_SPEED_DAMPENING` so the vehicle feels\\nheavier in water than on land.\\n\\nTwo forces do the work: `subMovementForce` drives lateral and forward motion\\nin the vehicle\'s own frame, and `subAntiGravity` carries the neutral-buoyancy\\nbaseline (`mass * gravity`) plus the vertical command on top. Because vertical\\ncontrol is an offset around neutral buoyancy, releasing the controls leaves the\\nvehicle hovering rather than sinking.","params":[{"name":"deltaTime","desc":"Frame delta from Heartbeat","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":927,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"update","desc":"Per-frame driver bound to Heartbeat by [VehicleController.startControl].\\nHandles what is common to both modes, then dispatches to\\n[VehicleController.updateCar] or [VehicleController.updateSubmarine].\\n\\n**Idle station-keeping.** After `CAR_IDLE_TIME` with no input, a submarine\\nengages its `AlignPosition` and re-anchors the hold point every 0.2s. That is\\nwhat stops a released submarine from drifting with residual velocity; a car\\nneeds no equivalent because friction handles it.\\n\\n**Empty seat.** If nobody is in the driver\'s seat, throttle is zeroed and all\\nfour wheels are held at zero velocity with full torque, and the frame ends\\nthere \u2014 an unoccupied vehicle brakes rather than coasting. This is a safety\\nnet for the window between the occupant leaving and\\n[VehicleController.stopControl] running.","params":[{"name":"deltaTime","desc":"Frame delta from Heartbeat","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1056,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"showPrompts","desc":"Enables or disables the vehicle\'s enter prompt. Turned off while driving so\\nthe prompt does not sit on screen in front of the seated player.","params":[{"name":"value","desc":"`true` to show the prompt","lua_type":"boolean"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1144,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"isControllingVehicle","desc":"Whether this client is currently driving. Other systems use this to suppress\\nbehaviour that would conflict with driving.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1161,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"carLookAt","desc":"Rotates the vehicle to face `position` over a one-second eased tween, keeping\\nit level \u2014 the target is flattened onto the vehicle\'s own Y plane, so this\\nonly ever changes yaw.\\n\\nImplemented by tweening a scratch `CFrameValue` and piping its `Changed` into\\n`PivotTo`, since models cannot be tweened directly. All three temporaries are\\ncleaned up afterwards.\\n\\n**Yields** until the tween completes.","params":[{"name":"position","desc":"World point to face","lua_type":"Vector3"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1181,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"isLookingInDirectionOfPosition","desc":"Whether the vehicle is roughly pointed at `position`. Both the vehicle\'s look\\nvector and the direction to the target are flattened to the horizontal plane,\\nso pitch is ignored; the test is `dot > LOOK_ANGLE` (0.95), about an 18\xb0 cone.","params":[{"name":"position","desc":"World point to test against","lua_type":"Vector3"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1223,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"setCarAnchoring","desc":"Anchors or un-anchors the vehicle by toggling `Anchored` on the driver\'s seat,\\nwhich is the assembly\'s root \u2014 anchoring the seat freezes the whole vehicle.\\nUsed to pin a vehicle in place for scripted moments.","params":[{"name":"state","desc":"`true` to anchor","lua_type":"boolean"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1249,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}},{"name":"spawn","desc":"Toggle handler for the spawn button: despawns the current vehicle if one is\\nlive, otherwise finds a legal spot and asks the server to spawn one.\\nDebounced, so a double-tap cannot fire two requests.\\n\\nPlacement is resolved entirely client-side before the request goes out, in two\\nsteps:\\n\\n1. **Ground find.** A point `SPAWN_DISTANCE` studs in front of the player is\\n   raycast straight down (from 10 studs up, 100 studs deep) to find the floor.\\n   No floor means no spawn \u2014 this is what stops a vehicle appearing over a\\n   ledge or above water.\\n2. **Clearance check.** A temporary invisible part the size of the car model\'s\\n   bounding box is placed at the resolved spot and `GetPartsInPart` is run\\n   against it. Any hit aborts.\\n\\nBoth queries filter against the same list of `Spawner`- and `Water`-tagged\\ninstances, so spawn pads and water do not count as obstructions. The car is\\ndropped 2 studs above the floor hit and raised by half its own height, keeping\\nits original yaw.\\n\\nThe server re-validates; this check exists to give immediate feedback and to\\navoid spamming rejected requests.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1289,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[],"name":"VehicleController","desc":"Handles client-side vehicle physics (Ackermann steering, throttle,\\nsubmarine mode), input, and distance tracking.\\n\\n### Why the physics is client-side\\n\\nThe server owns *existence* \u2014 spawning, despawning, seat authority, and the\\ndistance stat \u2014 while the driver\'s own client owns *motion*. The client that\\noccupies the `DriverSeat` has network ownership of the assembly anyway, so\\nsimulating there is both authoritative in practice and latency-free. The\\nserver is told only the outcome (`VEHICLE_LOG_DISTANCE` on dismount).\\n\\n### Singleton, not per-vehicle\\n\\nThis is a module-level singleton holding **one** `car` at a time \u2014 the vehicle\\nthis client may drive. [VehicleController.setupCar] overwrites that reference\\nwholesale. Other players\' vehicles are not tracked at all; their enter prompt\\nis simply destroyed so they cannot be boarded.\\n\\n### Two states\\n\\nA vehicle is either `driving` or `submarine`, switched by\\n[VehicleController.setState] off the character\'s `Swimming` attribute. The two\\nmodes drive completely different mechanisms and only one is ever live:\\n\\n- **driving** \u2014 four `CylindricalConstraint` wheel motors plus two front\\n  spring attachments used as steering knuckles. Torque on, flight constraints\\n  off.\\n- **submarine** \u2014 an `AlignOrientation`/`AlignPosition`/`VectorForce` rig that\\n  flies the chassis; the camera becomes the control surface. Torque zeroed,\\n  wheel motors idle.\\n\\n### Update pipeline\\n\\n[VehicleController.startControl] binds [VehicleController.update] to Heartbeat.\\nEach frame `update` handles the shared concerns \u2014 idle detection, station\\nkeeping, and cutting power when the seat is empty \u2014 then delegates to\\n[VehicleController.updateCar] or [VehicleController.updateSubmarine].\\n\\n### Steering geometry\\n\\nWheelbase and track width are measured from the *actual* constraint\\nattachments in [VehicleController.setupCar] using `Magnitude`, so they are\\nrotation-invariant and a re-authored car model needs no code change.\\n\\nGated by [FeatureFlags].Vehicle \u2014 disabled by default; per-project forks\\nenable it deliberately. Both [VehicleController.init] and\\n[VehicleController.start] return immediately when the flag is off, so nothing\\nis tagged, bound or subscribed.\\n\\nCopyright (c) 2026 firebit. All rights reserved.\\nfirebit/murder-escape - proprietary and confidential.","tags":["dormant"],"realm":["Client"],"source":{"line":58,"path":"src/Client/Features/Vehicle/Controllers/VehicleController.luau"}}')}}]);